      "pipeline_version": "quote_menu_v2",
      "question": "What is the default timeout in HTTPX?",
      "version": "0.28.1",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "The default timeout in HTTPX is five seconds for network inactivity.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "evidence_id": "E2",
              "quote_id": "Q2",
              "quote": "The default timeout for network inactivity is five seconds. You can modify the\nvalue to be more or less strict:",
              "chunk_id": "84c4aad941b6d1e060fb0ab5",
              "version": "0.28.1",
              "section": "QuickStart > Timeouts",
              "text": "## Timeouts\n\nHTTPX defaults to including reasonable timeouts for all network operations,\nmeaning that if a connection is not properly established then it should always\nraise an error rather than hanging indefinitely.\n\nThe default timeout for network inactivity is five seconds. You can modify the\nvalue to be more or less strict:\n\n```pycon\n>>> httpx.get('https://github.com/', timeout=0.001)\n```\n\nYou can also disable the timeout behavior completely...\n\n```pycon\n>>> httpx.get('https://github.com/', timeout=None)\n```\n\nFor advanced timeout management, see [Timeout fine-tuning](advanced/timeouts.md#fine-tuning-the-configuration).\n",
              "source_id": "httpx:0.28.1:docs/quickstart.md",
              "source_sha256": "9f8351551dd18be0ed7e40dea2f1c231523a2e8833a0bb5c471630178ec2aea8",
              "upstream_commit": "26d48e0634e6ee9cdc0533996db289ce4b430177",
